d They Came from Beyond the Grave! would be Mexican masked wrestlers who fight crab people and Aztec vampires. And probably alien space robots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T18:52:27-07:00","id":1404497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beyond-the-grave/1360217-they-came-from-beyond-the-grave?p=1404406#post1404406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If we get our Monsters from the Crypt book, expect psychics aplenty!</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! Can\u2019t wait \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T18:53:07-07:00","id":1404498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beyond-the-grave/1360217-they-came-from-beyond-the-grave?p=1404493#post1404493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me that the perfect crossover between They Came from Beneath the Sea! and They Came from Beyond the Grave! would be Mexican masked wrestlers who fight crab people and Aztec vampires. And probably alien space robots.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope they do a crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T19:22:39-07:00","id":1404503,"title":"","content":"As a random question for those who have supported They Came From Beneath the Sea is there Atlantis stuff in it? (I didn't back that as the more comedy aspects of that book didn't really super interest me and so if there is Atlantis using the Storypath system I will be sad that I missed it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T19:25:38-07:00","id":1404504,"title":"","content":"I kind of want a 70s/80s They Came from Beyond the Stars! and a 80s/90s They Came from Behind the Computer Screen! just to try to work out an ongoing campaign about a group that starts out fighting sea monsters/kaiju and progresses to cults/vampires/ghosts to aliens/robots/mutants to out of control AIs/rogue super hackers/Y2K. And clearly it should have earlier settings as well, but I'm not sure what the best ideas are for 20s/30s and 1900s/10s. Lovecraft feels a little too easy for the former and I'm not sure about the latter. Maybe They Came from Before Time! about prehistoric civilizations like Atlantis or Conan, lost races of serpent people, ancient astronauts, larger than life supermen (and women) and the like for the between war period. And perhaps They Came from the Center of the Earth for the earlier one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 07-24-2020, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T20:13:24-07:00","id":1404511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beyond-the-grave/1360217-they-came-from-beyond-the-grave?p=1404503#post1404503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a random question for those who have supported They Came From Beneath the Sea is there Atlantis stuff in it? (I didn't back that as the more comedy aspects of that book didn't really super interest me and so if there is Atlantis using the Storypath system I will be sad that I missed it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a Monster race called the Atlanteans (I think; it\u2019s been a while since I read the manuscript). I believe they are a race of water-breathing humans descended from the lost civilization of Atlantis who are planning an invasion of the surface world. I just got my backer copy a few weeks ago, so if you want I could look it up for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T20:36:09-07:00","id":1404514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beyond-the-grave/1360217-they-came-from-beyond-the-grave?p=1404126#post1404126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, anyone even remotely interested in this game who has never seen the 70s tv series <a href=\"https://www.nbc.com/kolchak-the-night-stalker/episodes\" target=\"_blank\">Kolchak the Night Stalker</a> really should do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. The sort of standard format for the game is one-shot movies that you're playing through. However, the Director's chapter also features tips on making a series, to delve into thinks like Kolchak and Dark Shadows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#990000\">Joshua Alan Doetsch</span></b><br /> <b>Freelance Writer<br /> <a href=\"http://joshuadoetsch.com/\" target=\"_blank\">joshuadoetsch.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1054-scrivnomancer","name":"scrivnomancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1054_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T11:38:14-07:00","id":1404607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beyond-the-grave/1360217-they-came-from-beyond-the-grave?p=1404511#post1404511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a Monster race called the Atlanteans (I think; it\u2019s been a while since I read the manuscript). I believe they are a race of water-breathing humans descended from the lost civilization of Atlantis who are planning an invasion of the surface world. I just got my backer copy a few weeks ago, so if you want I could look it up for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the information and the offer, I appreciate it. The fact that there is something probably means that I will be buying the book once its on pod cause I doubt I would miss this now that I see the potential of it in this new book. <br /> <br /> As a general question, how different/equal is this to the version of Storypath in Trinity. I mean could stuff from these books be used in a Trinity game with little work or a lot of work or something in between.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T16:26:29-07:00","id":1404665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beyond-the-grave/1360217-they-came-from-beyond-the-grave?p=1404607#post1404607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the information and the offer, I appreciate it. The fact that there is something probably means that I will be buying the book once its on pod cause I doubt I would miss this now that I see the potential of it in this new book. <br /> <br /> As a general question, how different/equal is this to the version of Storypath in Trinity. I mean could stuff from these books be used in a Trinity game with little work or a lot of work or something in between.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as l can tell the basic Storypath system is the same and you could convert characters and monsters from one to the other with relatively little effort. Special stuff like Quips might require a little more effort to convert to Trinity.<br /> <br /> Defo pick it up when it comes out on DTRPG. It\u2019s a really cool game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T17:27:36-07:00","id":1404679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beyond-the-grave/1360217-they-came-from-beyond-the-grave?p=1404665#post1404665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as l can tell the basic Storypath system is the same and you could convert characters and monsters from one to the other with relatively little effort. Special stuff like Quips might require a little more effort to convert to Trinity.<br /> <br /> Defo pick it up when it comes out on DTRPG. It\u2019s a really cool game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting and yeah I will. I honestly past it by when I heard humor and such things as that sort of game didn't really interest me. Buuut I am seeing so much in this one that makes me think that it would be easy to get past the aspects of the other one with little difficulty. <br /> <br /> Now I just have to wait for the Sea! book to come out so I can buy it in pdf and pod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T22:27:11-07:00","id":1404706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beyond-the-grave/1360217-they-came-from-beyond-the-grave?p=1404607#post1404607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a general question, how different/equal is this to the version of Storypath in Trinity. I mean could stuff from these books be used in a Trinity game with little work or a lot of work or something in between.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only know <b>Trinity</b> from reading the corebook, but from what I understand - ALL of <b>They Came From</b> stuff can be used as it is, without rule changes. Rewrites are Momentum ( directly ), Quips are system agnostic and Cinematics are based on Rewrites. Generally, <b>They Came From</b> are very rules-light games - they are MADE for one-shots and convention games foremost. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T22:31:04-07:00","id":1404708,"title":"","content":"We achive <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/they-came-from-beyond-the-grave/posts/2903847\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Monsters From the Crypt</b> supplement</a> with new antagonists! Next strech goals are backer t-shirts and doubling the size of <b>Monsters From the Crypt</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T13:18:12-07:00","id":1404822,"title":"","content":"Will Monsters from the Crypt be available as PoD or is it too early to say?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T07:13:20-07:00","id":1404915,"title":"","content":"Generally OPP releases the companion books as PoD. A document would have to be pamphlet size or smaller to not get a PoD release, usually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T05:56:34-07:00","id":1405052,"title":"","content":"Any chance of a stat bloc for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Sp-Rq6GyfLs\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Sp-Rq6GyfLs</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T21:57:31-07:00","id":1405246,"title":"","content":"We unlocked extra content for <b>Monsters From the Crypt!</b> suplement. At 39k $ we will get official wallpaper for all backers - and at 41k $ we get a new adventure in scenario supplement - <b>Tales of Depravity!</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-30-2020, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T14:45:58-07:00","id":1406331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beyond-the-grave/1360217-they-came-from-beyond-the-grave?p=1405246#post1405246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We unlocked extra content for <b>Monsters From the Crypt!</b> suplement. At 39k $ we will get official wallpaper for all backers - and at 41k $ we get a new adventure in scenario supplement - <b>Tales of Depravity!</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depravity is always a good thing! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T06:01:36-07:00","id":1407282,"title":"","content":"So far I think Beyond the Grave has a much richer and more detailed setting than Beneath the Sea, but maybe it\u2019s just that I prefer Beyond the Grave\u2019s genre and time periods. (I also think it\u2019s cool how in Beyond the Grave the example character and her boyfriend used to do it in the woods.)<br /> <br /> Are there any kaiju (giant monsters like Godzilla) in Beneath the Sea? I haven\u2019t looked at my copy in a while but I don\u2019t remember any except a giant squid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T06:04:34-07:00","id":1407283,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2176_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2176\" data-vbnamecard=\"2176\">SpectacularTentacular</a> \u201cA girl or boy cannot truly be considered depraved until they\u2019ve been to the best schools...\u201d<br /> <br /> A Victorian writer named H.H. Munro (Saki)<br /> <br /> Couldn\u2019t resist throwing that in lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T14:05:54-07:00","id":1407368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beyond-the-grave/1360217-they-came-from-beyond-the-grave?p=1407282#post1407282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any kaiju (giant monsters like Godzilla) in Beneath the Sea? I haven\u2019t looked at my copy in a while but I don\u2019t remember any except a giant squid.</div> </div> </div> </div>King sea serpents are hundreds of feet long (Size scale 3.) So, I think they'd count. The Bonnella Viridis Terribilus are something like Size scale 5. So, they are even bigger than King sea serpents. And the Centopus (not the squid you referenced) is Size scale 6! (Gargantuan squids are &quot;only&quot; size scale 3.) Mariner's Menace is Size scale 5. (Actually, most of the Primordial antagonists are size scale 3+.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T14:31:19-07:00","id":1407375,"title":"","content":"Thanks. That\u2019s really helpful.<br /> <br /> Can you define what exactly a Primordial antagonist is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 08-10-2020, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T14:37:21-07:00","id":1407377,"title":"","content":"Kaiju would be a creature scale 3 (like Skull Island Kong, around a hundred feet tall) or 4 (like Godzilla from 2014, a more than few hundred feet). Scale 6 creature is as big as an entire city.<br /> I would put Cthulhu on Scale 5 (around 1k feet tall), that is the one monstrous monster I really miss in BCFBTS!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T14:41:37-07:00","id":1407378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beyond-the-grave/1360217-they-came-from-beyond-the-grave?p=1407375#post1407375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. That\u2019s really helpful.<br /> <br /> Can you define what exactly a Primordial antagonist is?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is one of the thematic categories of antagonists in the book. If you have access to the PDF, you can find a heading in the antagonists chapter called Primordials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T14:58:30-07:00","id":1407384,"title":"","content":"I do have it. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T18:03:17-07:00","id":1407405,"title":"","content":"Wow!!! I just reread the Setting and Creatures chapters of TCFBTS. This game is really good, much better than I remember from the Kickstarter. There are A LOT of creatures, but they\u2019re all really interesting and they all kind of fit together into a coherent whole. Plus there\u2019s actually a couple pages about the shore town I used to summer at, including the candy store I got fudge from as a kid and the amusement park I hung out with my friends at when I got a little older. Definitely an awesome game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T18:56:37-07:00","id":1407415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beyond-the-grave/1360217-they-came-from-beyond-the-grave?p=1407405#post1407405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow!!! I just reread the Setting and Creatures chapters of TCFBTS. This game is really good, much better than I remember from the Kickstarter. There are A LOT of creatures, but they\u2019re all really interesting and they all kind of fit together into a coherent whole. Plus there\u2019s actually a couple pages about the shore town I used to summer at, including the candy store I got fudge from as a kid and the amusement park I hung out with my friends at when I got a little older. Definitely an awesome game.</div> </div> </div> </div>And never happened to find the Shrimp boy?<br /> <br /> Jokes apart, I never think about the cities in books as real cities, even the cities I have visited. Like, finding that one candy store you grow up is completely unimaginable to me, but it happens... interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T04:40:28-07:00","id":1407483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beyond-the-grave/1360217-they-came-from-beyond-the-grave?p=1407415#post1407415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And never happened to find the Shrimp boy?<br /> <br /> Jokes apart, I never think about the cities in books as real cities, even the cities I have visited. Like, finding that one candy store you grow up is completely unimaginable to me, but it happens... interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Made out with him at the amusement park after we both had a slice of shrimp pizza lol (they really do serve that at the pizzeria next door)<br /> <br /> But seriously. I was amazed. It\u2019s not that big of a town and most people have never heard of it, plus I was amazed that the candy store I used to love was still around back in the Fifties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T18:07:29-07:00","id":1408081,"title":"","content":"Interesting is how are Ghosts and other immaterial threats done in <b>Beyond the Grave</b> - Ghosts have Might and Stamina 0 and they pay for their powers and interactions with their Health. Of course, they can also regain Health by doing some things...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-14-2020, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T18:09:07-07:00","id":1408082,"title":"","content":"I love <b>Beyond The Grave</b> for joking about the prudish society of the 1970s West. (And I suppose modern Poland. \ud83d\ude09) 'Devil Worshipers come in many forms, from the erudite gentleman in a crimson cloak to the rock enthusiast leading our children into sin. Sin! Turn away from Blue \u00d6yster Cult while you can! ' Blue \u00d6yster Cult as messengers of Satan! \ud83d\ude03\ud83d\ude04\ud83d\ude01","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-15-2020, 02:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T23:30:30-07:00","id":1408106,"title":"","content":"Hunted House stats <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/k2dIFua.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T03:01:32-07:00","id":1408120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beyond-the-grave/1360217-they-came-from-beyond-the-grave?p=1408106#post1408106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunted House stats <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/k2dIFua.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02<br /> <br /> I still have to read my preview","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T17:48:10-07:00","id":1408429,"title":"","content":"I read the preview. I liked the Monsters, especially the Devil Worshipper (I know guys and girls like that), and I thought it was cool that Dracula got his powers from The Devil Himself, but I wish the Settings part had included more specific detailed locations and ideas instead of just generic sets (like I liked how in TCFBTS they made Joseph Stalin a superintelligent zombie). <br /> <br /> Also, in the sample character creation chapter they made a big deal about tying the two games together, and I was disappointed they didn\u2019t follow through with that in the setting chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T18:21:51-07:00","id":1408435,"title":"","content":"One more thing<br /> <br /> You guys were probably just making fun of Seventies pop culture, but Blue Cheer\u2019s not a Satanic band. I read about them in a history book one time. They were a REALLY sucky acid rock band, so bad they were famous for it. Maybe you meant Blue Oyster Cult?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T20:21:00-07:00","id":1408448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beyond-the-grave/1360217-they-came-from-beyond-the-grave?p=1408429#post1408429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read the preview. I liked the Monsters, especially the Devil Worshipper (I know guys and girls like that), and I thought it was cool that Dracula got his powers from The Devil Himself, but I wish the Settings part had included more specific detailed locations and ideas instead of just generic sets (like I liked how in TCFBTS they made Joseph Stalin a superintelligent zombie).<br /> <br /> Also, in the sample character creation chapter they made a big deal about tying the two games together, and I was disappointed they didn\u2019t follow through with that in the setting chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>But are there Blackulas? Because I don't want to live in a 1970s horror movie world without Blackulas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T22:42:55-07:00","id":1408461,"title":"","content":"No lol. No Blaculas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T12:40:09-07:00","id":1408767,"title":"","content":"Seriously though, it's weird title aside, Blackula is a pretty solid classic-style (ie pre-80s) vampire movie. It's up there along side the classic Hammer Horror films, Kolchak the Night Stalker, the Ira Levin trilogy of Rosemary's Baby, The Stepford Wives, and The Boys from Brazil, and Marvel's Tomb of Dracula series on the list of stuff I hope this game can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T10:32:43-07:00","id":1408970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beyond-the-grave/1360217-they-came-from-beyond-the-grave?p=1408767#post1408767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously though, it's weird title aside, Blackula is a pretty solid classic-style (ie pre-80s) vampire movie. It's up there along side the classic Hammer Horror films, Kolchak the Night Stalker, the Ira Levin trilogy of Rosemary's Baby, The Stepford Wives, and The Boys from Brazil, and Marvel's Tomb of Dracula series on the list of stuff I hope this game can do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm a fan of Blackula! Francois Mamuwalde even shows up in Chicago by Night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0